WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
4 February.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.630
Using Global Footprint
Network's 2024 data:

3
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.230
live like the average person in Qatar,
and humanity uses up a year's worth of

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.610
nature by then.

5
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:16.870
Live like the average person in India, and
the year's supply lasts the whole year.

6
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.770
Like Bangladesh, and humanity
uses just 46 per cent of it.

7
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.890
So what is being measured?

8
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.010
Is it oil?

9
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:25.710
Money?

10
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.810
How crowded each country is?

11
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.170
In this mission, you'll
track Earth Overshoot Day,

12
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.750
from 31 December 1972 to 30 July 2026.

13
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.310
Then you'll ask why the date announced
in 2026 was later than the one announced

14
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.470
in 2025, and what one measure can prove.

15
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.290
Your mission: work out what a
year's worth of nature means,

16
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.760
and how it is measured.
